  "review_text": "[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=extralarge; text=<b>1964 End of the Year Review</b>]\nNew to the awards?&nbsp; See the [PAGE: awards-index] for full descriptions.\n\n[DIVIDER]\n1964 brought us <b>????</b> new books -- not counting [PAGE: meanwhile] -- containing <b>????</b> actually reviewed and graded stories.\n\n<b>FIXME - rewrite all this!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</b>\n\nThe output nearly doubled in terms of actually-published issues from 1963 to 1964 (???? to ????) and <i>more</i> than doubled in terms of stories (???? to ????), though the total <i>weight</i> was only just over ???? (meaning just over ???? full-sized books times 20 pages worth of material -- it means that there were a <i>lot</i> of partial books on the shelves this year).\n\nIn the end, the final weighted average was [SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx], which included ???? stories that were at least mid-grade (6.0 or better), though ???? (nearly double) were <i>below</i> readable (less than 4.0), so the net result was that, while stories <i>could</i> occasionally be good, [SPAN: severity=warning; text=readers were forced to sift through a lot of baggage to find them.]\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Introductions</b>]\n\nMajor introductions included:\n[HANG] *\n\nThe year also introduced other characters such as XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Top Moments of the Year</b>]\n[HANG] * Captain America is \"resurrected\" by the Avengers after 20 years in suspended animation -- <i>surely</i> one of Marvel's all-time highlights!\n[HANG] *\n\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Other Notable Observations about the Year</b>]\n[HANG] *\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: severity=success; display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Best Story of the Year</b>]\n\n\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: severity=error; display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Trash Heap of the Year</b>]\n\n[HANG0] ??\n\nThus, it is [SPAN: severity=error; fontsize=larger; fonttype=bold; text=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx] that takes the... <i>uh</i>... \"bottom\" spot this year!\n\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: severity=error; display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Shaft Award</b>]\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Top Covers</b>]\n\n[HANG] * [LINK:1964:AVEN_4|AVEN #4|2027-04-25] -- Who will <i>ever </i>forget \"Captain America Lives Again!\"&nbsp; It's one for the history books (and a darn good cover to boot)!\n\nSo I award the honor to [SPAN: severity=success; fontsize=larger; fonttype=bold; text=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx].\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Best Panel of the Year</b>]\n\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Best Back-Up Story</b>]\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Best Belly-Laugh Moment</b>]\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Biggest Blunder</b>]\n\n[HANG] * ??\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Best Credit Box</b>]\n\n[ASSET: left | CreditsJIM102 | width=12%] This is the year where we begin to start seeing more playful credits, such as this example (from [LINK:1964:JIM_102_thor0|JIM #102|2027-04-28]).\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Biggest Surprise of the Year</b>]\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Spiral Award</b>]\n\n[HANG0] [LINK:1964:ST_119_torch1|ST #119torch|2027-05-13] -- the Human Torch goes from hero to fugitive in 3 pages during a forgettable encounter with the \"Rabble Rouser.\"\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Best and Worst Things to Happen to Marvel This Year</b>]\n\nThe [SPAN: severity=success; text=best thing] for this year was xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\nAs for the [SPAN: severity=error; text=worst thing], I have to go with xxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Trope of the Year</b>]\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>State of the Line Report</b>]\n\nBelow is the list of characters who have their own feature, sorted from best to worst in terms of average grade.\n\nSpider-Man (<b>x.xx</b>)\n[BR] Fantastic Four (<b>x.xx</b>)\n[BR] Iron Man (<b>x.xx</b>)\n[BR] Ant/Giant-Man (<b>x.xx</b>)\n[BR] Thor (<b>x.xx</b>)\n[BR] Doctor Strange (<b>x.xx</b>)\n[BR] Human Torch (<b>x.xx</b>)\n\nSpider-Man (<b>9xxx</b>)\n[BR] Fantastic Four (<b>14.33xxx</b>)\n[BR] Iron Man (<b>7xxx</b>)\n[BR] Ant/Giant-Man (<b>6.75xxx</b>)\n[BR] Thor (<b>6xxx</b>)\n[BR] Doctor Strange (<b>2.07xxx</b>)\n[BR] Human Torch (<b>7xxx</b>)\n\n\n\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[SPAN: display=block; fontsize=large; text=<b>Overall Impression</b>]"
